The model repository declares Apache-2.0 and contains the corresponding LICENSE.
Its pretrained ECAPA512 component is attributed to WeSpeaker/VoxCeleb. There is
a licensing discrepancy: the Hugging Face ECAPA512 card declares Apache-2.0,
while official WeSpeaker pretrained-model documentation states CC BY 4.0 for
VoxCeleb-trained weights. Component/model redistribution needs a separate audit;
this source change does not redistribute any model weights.
https://github.com/wenet-e2e/wespeaker/blob/master/docs/pretrained.md#model-license
https://huggingface.co/Wespeaker/wespeaker-voxceleb-ecapa-tdnn512

ONNX Runtime C API is used as an external native dependency (not vendored here).
ONNX Runtime is Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation, MIT License.
Runtime binary distributions require their LICENSE and ThirdPartyNotices.txt.
No VoxLock demonstration recordings, benchmark audio or ONNX Runtime binary are
included in this source change. Audio fixtures retain their own dataset licenses.

Enrollment magnitude/context are private derived acoustic data, potentially
retaining reconstructable speech. They must be handled like a voice recording.
This diagnostic backend has no target-absence gate and cannot promise that an
absent owner's profile suppresses every other speaker. No app integration yet.
